{
 "title": "Geometry nodes 7: a house",
 "summary": "A house generator in geometry nodes, on a cube whose top face is extruded into a roof: walls found by comparing face normals (not up, not down, Boolean Math AND) take the house material; a window modelled in nodes (a subdivided cube, its front and back faces inset with Extrude Mesh + Scale Elements and pushed in) is instanced on every wall face (Capture Attribute of the normal, Mesh to Points on faces, Align Euler to Vector) and cut into the walls with Mesh Boolean; roof tiles (a half circle extruded and solidified) are instanced on a grid above the house raycast down onto the roof. Beyond the tutorial: the same node group on a long house and a two-storey one, tiles running down each slope, a stone plinth from the Bounding Box.",
 "objects": [
  {
   "name": "House",
   "description": ""
  },
  {
   "name": "HouseLong",
   "description": ""
  },
  {
   "name": "HouseTall",
   "description": ""
  }
 ],
