   "note": "the house's Geometry Nodes: walls picked by their normals (Compare vectors, not up and not down, epsilon wide enough to drop the sloping roof faces, Boolean Math AND) get the house material, the rest the roof's; a window built from a cube (Subdivide Mesh, its front and back faces picked by Normal == +Y OR -Y, Extrude Mesh at 0 and Scale Elements on the Top: an inset, then extruded -0.08 into the frame, frame and glass materials) is instanced on every wall face (Capture Attribute of the face Normal, Mesh to Points in Faces mode, Align Euler to Vector) and subtracted from the walls with Mesh Boolean; the roof tiles are instanced on a Grid raised above the house and Raycast down onto it (Set Position to the Hit Position, only where Is Hit and the face isn't flat), laid on the roof by the Hit Normal. Beyond the tutorial: the tiles also turn to run down each slope, and a stone plinth comes from the house's Bounding Box",
